ually there's a subtle issue: the \"Components\" page says \"Components · Meet (default states only)\" — the Button is a component with default state. The brief says design all other states as reusable components. I'll create my own components in the workspace for everything custom.\n\nOne more consideration: overriding icon colors inside instances. When I create an instance of Icon_Back (component 5:26) and want it white, I need to set the vector's stroke/fill color inside the instance. Let me check what the icons look like first — I should get design context for one icon to understand its structure (fills vs strokes).\n\nAlso for portraits — they're components containing images presumably as fills on rectangles. I can instance and resize/crop as needed. For different sizes (e.g., story avatar 56px circle, card image full-width), I can scale instances. Since they're components with image fills, resizing the instance will stretch unless I handle it. Let me check the structure of a portrait component first.\n\nLet me get design context for key components:\n- Button 1:28\n- Status Bar 1:33, Home Indicator 1:44\n- One portrait e.g. 5:112 (Portrait_Aidan)\n- One icon e.g. 5:26 (Icon_Back)\n- Logo 5:4\n\nActually, get_design_context gives XML with details. Let me fetch a few in parallel. Note the reminder: \"After you call this tool, you MUST call get_design_context if trying to implement the design\" — I've been using get_metadata for reference pages which is fine, but for implementation I need get_design_context. Let me now use get_design_context on the key nodes.\n\nAlso check workspace page 7:2 metadata.\n\nLet me batch: get_design_context for 1:28 (Button), 1:33 (Status Bar), 1:44 (Home Indicator), 5:112 (Portrait_Aidan), 5:26 (Icon_Back), 5:4 (Logo_Meet), and metadata for 7:2 (workspace).\n\nActually get_design_context might return large payloads. Let me be judicious. The Button and shell are essential. Portrait structure is essential (image fill handling). Icon st