acity=1){\n  const paint = {type:\"SOLID\", color, opacity};\n  for(const v of inst.findAll(n=>n.type===\"VECTOR\"||n.type===\"BOOLEAN_OPERATION\"||n.type===\"STAR\"||n.type===\"ELLIPSE\"||n.type===\"RECTANGLE\"||n.type===\"LINE\")){\n    if(v.strokes && v.strokes.length && v.strokes[0].visible!==false) v.strokes=[paint];\n    else if(v.fills && Array.isArray(v.fills) && v.fills.length && v.fills[0].visible!==false && v.fills[0].type===\"SOLID\") v.fills=[paint];\n  }\n}\n```\nCareful: don't recolor brand icons (Facebook/Google) — skip recolor for those.\nAlso don't recolor portrait instances (image fills) — recolor only used on icon comps.\n\n**Text on instances**: story avatar instance: find text child by name → set characters (font already loaded in session — IMPORTANT: in each use_figma call, before setting characters on any text (including inside instances), the font of that text must be loaded — it's Inter, loaded).\n\n**Resizing icon button instances**: instance.resize(w,h) — children with CENTER constraints stay centered; icon 24 fixed. Good.\n\n**Tab bar component structure** (393×56):\n- bg rect white? Component root fill white, stroke? top hairline: child rect 393×1 border color at y=0.\n- 5 slots, center x: 39.3, 117.9, 196.5, 275.1, 353.7. Icon y=10 (24), label y=36 (11). For Add: circle 40 plum at y=8 center, Icon_Plus white 20 (instance resized 20×20? icon instance resize scales vectors? Instance resize resizes node bounds; vector child with SCALE constraint scales. Icon components' vectors constraints — unknown default (likely MIN). Resizing instance 24→20 without scaling child = icon stays 24 clipped! Risky. Instead keep 24 icon white on plum circle 44. y=6.\n- Active styling per variant: active icon color plum (except Add always plum circle; active Add? Add is never current in our screens — fine), label plum M; inactive ink3 R(11 Medium? label inactive 11 Medium ink3, active 11 Semi Bold plum?). Also active dot 4 orchid under label? Let me add smal