e Face ID reaction: target = the pill frame inside sheet instance (found by name \"Face ID Button\"). Setting reactions on node inside instance — allowed (override). OK.\n\nAlternatively attach reaction to the sheet instance's child... same thing.\n\nFallbacks with hotspots if setter throws.\n\n**Transition objects**: I'll write helper:\n```js\nfunction nav(destId, transition){ const t = transition || {type:\"INSTANT\"}; return {action:{type:\"NODE\", destinationId:destId, navigation:\"NAVIGATE\", transition:t}, trigger:{type:\"ON_TAP\"}}; }\n```\nTransitions: sheet up: {type:\"MOVE_IN\", direction:\"BOTTOM\", duration:0.3, easing:{type:\"EASE_OUT\"}}? Hmm easing objects: I've seen {type:\"EASE_OUT\"}? The official easing types: LINEAR, EASE_IN, EASE_OUT, EASE_IN_AND_OUT, GENTLE, QUICK, BOUNCY, CUSTOM_CUBIC_BEZIER, SMART... I'll use {type:\"GENTLE\"} (Figma's gentle curve) — I recall GENTLE/QUICK/BOUNCY are valid custom easing presets in the API. To be safe use EASE_IN_AND_OUT? Actually simplest safe: omit easing? Transition requires duration+easing for non-instant? Types: {type:\"DISSOLVE\", duration, easing?}. I'll include duration 0.3 and easing {type:\"EASE_OUT\"}; wrap reaction-setting in try/catch: on failure retry with {type:\"INSTANT\"}.\n\nActually — MOVE_IN/MOVE_OUT directions: \"LEFT\"|\"RIGHT\"|\"TOP\"|\"BOTTOM\". OK.\n\nLet me also double check **combineAsVariants** not used. Good.\n\n**One more check — creating COMPONENT nodes**: figma.createComponent(); comp.resizeWithoutConstraints(w,h); set name; append children; then to make it a real component node on page — createComponent returns COMPONENT node already. Append to section/page. Good.\n\n**Instances**: comp.createInstance().\n\n**IMPORTANT**: after building components, the section holds originals; instances go into frames.\n\n**Text auto-resize**: default createText autoResize is WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT (grows). For centered multi-line, set textAutoResize=\"HEIGHT\" + resize width + textAlignHorizontal C