unattended session — don't wait for human answers.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Build the complete design in 03 · Workspace (page 7:2, currently empty):\n     1. Define and apply my design tokens (neutrals, text colors, surfaces, overlays, semantic colors, type scale, spacing, radii) on brand #4B164C/#DD88CF + Inter.\n     2. Create custom reusable components in the workspace: platform tab bar (with current-tab state variants), headers, story avatars, feed post card, partner swipe card stack, action buttons, profile header, media grid tiles, short-video overlay, sign-in sheet, drawer, menu rows, and state designs (current tab, current profile tab, pressed, followed/liked, disabled).\n     3. Build the 8 frames named exactly: 01_Welcome, 02_Apple_ID_Sheet, 03_Explore, 04_Find_Partner, 05_Friend_Profile, 06_Short_Video, 07_Profile, 08_Menu (393×852 each; 02 sheet over 01 background; 08 drawer over 07 background; add Status Bar + Home Indicator on every frame, white-glyph overrides on dark screens).\n     4. Wire all prototype links listed in section 3 (Sign Up→02, Face ID→03, close→01, Claire story→05, Dating tab→04, Profile tab→07, back/Home→03, Short tab→06, menu→08, close/Show Profile→07).\n     5. Screenshot-verify every screen, fix visible problems, re-check.\n     6. Final answer with file URL, workspace page ID 7:2, screen node IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Just completed the read-only inspection phase. The last action was a read-only use_figma call returning detailed structures for Button (1:28: plum SOLID fill rgb(0.294,0.086,0.298), radius 26, child TEXT \"Use mobile number\" Inter Semi Bold 16 white), Status Bar (1:33: 393×54, black glyphs at stated positions), Home Indicator (1:44: 134×5 black r3 rect), Portrait_Aidan (5:112: COMPONENT 120×180 with direct IMAGE fill scaleMode FILL, no children), Icon_Back (5:26: 24×24, child VECTOR with stroke #1A1A1F weight 2), Logo_Meet (5:4: 34×35 vector plum fill). Workspace page 7:2 confirmed EMPTY. Nothing has been built yet — next phase is writing the workspace via use_figma.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Begin building in 03 · Workspace (page 7:2) via mcp__figma__use_figma, in manageable sections per the harness instruction \"Build in manageable sections and check tool results before continuing.\" Concretely, first build step: switch to page 7:2 (await figma.setCurrentPageAsync), create a component section with my custom reusable components (Tab Bar with 5 tabs and current-tab variants, headers, story avatar, feed post card, partner card, action buttons, profile header pieces, menu row, sheet/drawer containers), instancing given components (Button 1:28, Status Bar 1:33, Home Indicator 1:44, icons, portraits) as needed — then lay out the 8 frames, then wire prototypes, then screenshot-verify each frame. This directly continues the user's sole request: “最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」”, with every subsequent tool call still prefixed by \"Reasoning summary:\" as required.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /mnt/afs/huangxinyue/bench-runs/10case-6models-v4-20261101/runs/TEST-034_1793483368770/claude-config/projects/-mnt-afs-huangxinyue-bench-runs-10case-6models-v4-20261101-workspace/e49f7b8d-beff-4d45-bc73-771a1107ac68.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e49f7b8d-beff-4d45-bc73-771a1107ac68","uuid":"39565cd9-cb