arting points (frame). Interactions: `node.interactions`? Hmm. The plugin API: `PrototypeInteraction`? Actual API: node has `prototypeConnectors`? Let me recall: Plugin API has `node.prototypeStartNode` (boolean-ish? it's `node.prototypeStartNode = true`?). For interactions: `node.interactions = [{ trigger: {type: 'ON_TAP'}, action: {type: 'NODE', destinationId: '...'} }]`? \n\nThe Plugin API typing: `Interaction` interfaces exist: `node.interactions` is not standard. Actually there IS: `prototypeStartNode` on FrameNode (boolean). For connections: In the plugin API, interactions are exposed via `node.reactions`? Yes! `Reaction` = { trigger: Trigger (e.g. {type:'ON_TAP'}), action: Action }. Node.reactions: Reaction[]. And actions: { type: 'NODE', destinationId, navigation: 'NAVIGATE' | 'OVERLAY' etc. }. Trigger types: {type: 'ON_TAP'}, {type:'ON_PRESS'}. Navigation: navigation: 'NAVIGATE', transition: {type:'INSTANT'|'DISSOLVE'|...}.\n\nFor overlays: action { type: 'NODE', destinationId, navigation: 'OVERLAY', overlayPositionType: 'CENTER', ... }. But since 02 and 08 are separate frames replicating the background, use NAVIGATE with transition INSTANT or DISSOLVE. Brief says \"Presentation: sheet over 01\" — I've built them as full frames with background baked in, so NAVIGATE is fine.\n\nSo: node.reactions = [{ trigger: { type: 'ON_TAP' }, action: { type: 'NODE', destinationId: targetId, navigation: 'NAVIGATE', transition: { type: 'INSTANT' } } }]. Hmm trigger type name: 'ON_TAP' (v1) or {type: 'ON_DOWN'}? In plugin API docs: Trigger = { type: 'ON_TAP' } | { type:'ON_PRESS'} etc. I believe 'ON_TAP' is correct (used with MouseEventType?). Older API: trigger: { type: 'ON_CLICK' }? Let me think. Figma plugin typings: \n\n```\ndeclare type Trigger = \n  { type: 'ON_TAP' } | { type: 'ON_PRESS' } | ...\n```\n\nI recall from dev docs: `figma.currentPage.selection[0].reactions` example: `[{trigger: {type: 'ON_CLICK'}, action: {type: 'BACK'}}]`? Hmm. There's \"ON_TAP\" in the newer API and \"ON_CLICK\" deprecated. The typings file (plugin-typings) has:\n\n```\ntype Trigger = {\n  readonly type: 'ON_TAP' | 'ON_PRESS' | ... \n}\n```\n\nActually the official docs \"PrototypeNode\" say: node.reactions — Reaction[] where Reaction = { trigger: Trigger, action: Action } and Trigger = { type: \"ON_TAP\" } etc. I'm fairly confident 'ON_TAP' is valid in current typings. If it errors, try 'ON_CLICK'.\n\nAlso frame.prototypeStartNode = true for 01_Welcome (flow start).\n\nNow — output token management: I must write many use_figma calls with sizeable code. Keep each call ≤ ~8-10k chars code. Build order with per-call builds:\n\nCall A: Setup page + assets: create \"design tokens\" invisible? Skip tokens; straight to frames. Call A: build 01_Welcome + record its id. Also load fonts once per call (loadFontAsync needed in each call where text created).\n\nCommon helpers to re-declare in each call (functions can't persist between calls): \n\n```js\nconst P={r:0.294,g:0.086,b:0.298}; // plum\nconst OR={r:0.867,g:0.533,b:0.812}; // orchid\nconst INK={r:0.102,g:0.102,b:0.122};\nconst GRAY={r:0.42,g:0.42,b:0.463};\nconst BG={r:0.969,g:0.961,b:0.973};\nconst W={r:1,g:1,b:1};\nfunction S(c,a){return {type:'SOLID',color:c,opacity:a===undefined?1:a}}\nasync function comp(id){return await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)}\nasync function inst(id,x,y,w,h){const c=await comp(id);const n=c.createInstance();n.x=x;n.y=y;if(w!==undefined)n.resize(w,h||w* (c.height/c.width));return n}\nfunction txt(chars,size,font,color,x,y,w,align){...}\n```\n\nFont load: await figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter',style:'Bold'}) etc per call.\n\nText creation helper:\n```js\nfunction mkText(chars,size,style,color){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:'Inter',style};t.characters=chars;t.fontSize=size;t.fills=[S(color)];return t}\n```\nMust set fontName before characters, with font loaded.\n\nAlso note: page switching: `const page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('7:2'); await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);` — needed in first call; subsequent calls: current page persists? Each use_figma call is a fresh plugin execution but same editor session; current page persists across calls in the same session, but to be safe, set it each time (cheap).\n\nAlso appending to page: `page.appendChild(node)`.\n\nLet me also handle icon recolor helper:\n```js\nasync function icol(id,x,y,size,color,op){const n=await inst(id,x,y,size,size); n.findAll(c=>'strokes' in c && c.strokes.length>0).forEach(c=>c.strokes=[S(color,op)]); return n}\n```\nWait findAll on instance — allowed (findAll works on instances for reading; modifying instance children properties = overrides, allowed). Strokes override on vector children of instance: allowed.\n\nBut caution: Icon_Facebook and Icon_Google keep brand colors — don't recolor those.\n\nAlso Icon_Heart used with plum color on white badge — stroke recolor to plum.\n\nStatus bar recolor to white: instance 1:33, findAll texts and shapes with black fills/strokes → set white. Status bar children: \"9:41\" text (black fill), signal frame (fills black?), wifi ellipse fill black, battery strokes black + fill? Simplest: override ALL descendants: any fill black → white; any stroke black → white. Helper:\n```js\nfunction whiteSB(n){n.findAll(c=>{if('fills' in c && c.fills.length>0){c.fills=c.fills.map(f=>f.type==='SOLID'?{...f,color:W}:f)} if('strokes' in c && c.strokes.length>0){c.strokes=c.strokes.map(s=>s.type==='SOLID'?{...s,color:W}:s)}})}\n```\nCareful: dynamic island is black rect — on dark plum bg it can stay black (it's the device island) — fine either way; make it white? On real iOS island is black always. Keep island black; my blanket recolor would make it white — bad. So instead: recolor only fills that are exactly INK black {0.102,0.102,0.122}? Island fill: from summary \"Dynamic Island black rounded rect\" — likely #000000 or #1A1A1F. Glyphs black too. Hmm.\n\nSafer: recolor by node name? I don't have exact names for all children. Alternative: blanket recolor everything except nodes named containing \"Island\". Use c.name check: if /island/i.test(c.name) skip. Good enough.\n\nActually simpler: on dark screens, place status bar instance and recolor: glyphs white, island stays black. If island is #000 vs glyph #1A1A1F I can't distinguish reliably. Use name check.\n\nHome indicator white override similarly (child rect black→white) — name-agnostic (no island issue).\n\nTab bar helper (per frame, active index):\n```js\nasync function tabBar(x,y,active){ \n const f=figma.createFrame(); f.name='Tab Bar'; f.x=x;f.y=y;f.resize(393,82); f.fills=[S(W)]; \n // top hairline\n const line=figma.createRectangle(); line.resize(393,1); line.x=0;line.y=0; line.fills=[S({r:0.925,g:0.918,b:0.941})]; f.appendChild(line);\n const items=[['Home',homeIcon],['Dating',heart],['Add',plus],['Chat',chat],['Profile',sarah]]\n ...\n}\n```\nIcons needed: Icon_Home 5:36, Icon_Heart 5:17, Icon_Plus 5:39, Icon_Chat 5:42, Portrait_Sarah_Payne 5:123.\n\nFor active item color plum; inactive gray #8E8E99 (0.557,0.557,0.6)? Use GRAY.\n\nAdd tab special: Icon_Plus inside 40×40 circle bg light? When active (never active in our frames) — Add is never current. So Add: gray plus in circle #F1EDF4 (0.945,0.929,0.957).\n\nLabels: Inter Medium 10.\n\nProfile tab: portrait instance 24×24 cornerRadius 12; if active add 2px plum ring (stroke on a wrapping ellipse or the instance strokeColor). Instance cornerRadius works on images. Ring: ellipse 30 plum stroke behind? Simpler: set instance strokes=[S(P)] strokeWeight 2 when active.\n\nTab bar as component with variants would be ideal but heavy; build function reused in each call — fine (it's code reuse, not Figma reuse; acceptable per requirements since components \"allowed\" not mandated). Hmm — \"复用「02·Components」组件\" refers to given components — satisfied. But adding custom reusable components is a plus for the brief's spirit (\"reusable components are allowed\"). I'll create the Tab Bar