"t-profile\" (icons), \"l-home\"... For override: inst.findOne(n=>n.name==='t-dating') then set strokes. findOne on instance returns override-able child. \n\nNote: instance children of type INSTANCE (icon instances nested) — icon is an instance of Icon_Home inside tab bar component; recoloring its vector child = nested override; allowed via findAll on the icon instance child.\n\nProfile avatar active ring: override stroke on the avatar instance itself: inst.strokes=[S(P)] strokeWeight=2 strokeAlign 'OUTSIDE'.\n\nOK. Also \"Add\" circle fill override not needed (Add never active).\n\nFonts to load per call: Inter Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Bold (and maybe Extra Bold). Load once at start of each call (parallel awaits).\n\nNow specifics per frame with exact coordinates. Let me now write Call A: page setup + Tab Bar component. Keep code tight.\n\nActually, let me reconsider building order to parallelize independent things: 01 (B) and TabBar+03 (D) independent. But tool calls in same message run in parallel — Figma MCP probably serializes; parallel writes to same file could race. Safer sequential for writes. Reads/screenshots can batch.\n\nAlso — IMPORTANT: after building all, wire prototypes (call J) and set 01 as flow start (prototypeStartNode = true on frame 01).\n\nScreenshots: 8 frames. Batch in pairs to manage tokens: 4 messages × 2? Or one message with 4 parallel screenshot calls (each returns URL + maybe image if enableBase64 true). I need to SEE them: must enableBase64Response=true to view inline (I can't curl? I have no shell tool in this env! Tools available: only figma tools — no Bash. So I cannot download URLs via curl → must use enableBase64Response:true). Yes — enableBase64Response true required.\n\nToken budget: 15M total left, plenty.\n\nLet me write Call A now: setup + Tab Bar component.\n\nCode A:\n```js\nconst page = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('7:2');\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page);\nawait Promise.all([\n figma.loadFontAsync({family:'Inter'