{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The runtime's reaction schema differs from what I assumed. From the error messages, valid shapes:\n\nTrigger: `{type: 'ON_CLICK'}` is valid (enum: 'ON_CLICK' | 'ON_HOVER' | 'ON_PRESS' | 'ON_DRAG' | 'ON_MEDIA_END').\n\nAction NODE: The first variant listed expects... Looking at errors: action type 'NODE' failed. The listed options include 'CONDITIONAL', 'BACK'/'CLOSE', 'URL', 'UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME', 'SET_VARIABLE', 'SET_VARIABLE_MODE'. Interesting — there's no plain \"navigate to node\" option?? Wait — one of the messages says:\n\n```\nExpected [0].action.transition to be one of the following, but none matched:\n  ... Required value missing at [0].action.transition.easing / duration\n  Invalid enum value. Expected 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT', received 'DISSOLVE' ...\n```\n\nThat block mentions action.transition — which suggests there IS a navigate-type action that includes a transition, but my 'DISSOLVE' was invalid there and transition requires easing+duration. The navigate action in this schema is probably `{type:'NAVIGATE', destinationId, transition, ...}`? Hmm but the literal enum didn't list 'NAVIGATE'... Actually the error output is truncated/multiple \"one of the following\" groups. The group mentioning transition is likely the 'NAVIGATE' action variant. It says \"Unrecognized key(s) in object: 'destinationId', 'navigation', 'transition'\" for type 'NODE' — because 'NODE' isn't valid; the navigate variant probably has type 'NAVIGATE' with destinationId and transition directly (no 'navigation' key).\n\nSo try: action = {type:'NAVIGATE', destinationId: dest, transition: {type:'DISSOLVE', duration:0.3, easing:{type:'EASE_IN_OUT'}}}? But the transition enum for that variant expects 'MOVE_IN' | 'MOVE_OUT' | 'PUSH' | 'SLIDE_IN' | 'SLIDE_OUT'?? That's for directional transitions. And another sub-variant requires easing+duration (that's INSTANT? no...). Hmm, the err