{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__get_screenshot, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a Figma product design benchmark. The user's sole request (Chinese): 在 Figma 文件 https://www.figma.com/design/vnQfW15mcjOlAJYP4Lrvrx/ 中完成完整设计——先阅读「00·Start Here」设计任务，参考「01·Foundations」视觉规范，复用「02·Components」组件，使用「04·Media」素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。\n\n   Binding benchmark harness rules:\n   - Use only assigned file (fileKey vnQfW15mcjOlAJYP4Lrvrx); account confirmed via whoami as zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (DONE earlier).\n   - Preserve all reference pages (00/01/02/04) and their nodes; keep unrelated content intact; never create a different file or switch accounts/teams.\n   - Build the complete design in 03 · Workspace (page 7:2); new frames/components/prototype connections allowed there.\n   - Build exactly 8 frames with exact names, exact must-include content and copy (verbatim), Inter font only, brand colors #4B164C + #DD88CF, reuse given components as instances, wire listed prototype links, add Status Bar + Home Indicator to every frame.\n   - Verify every screen via screenshots; fix visible problems; screenshot success alone ≠ completion — finish all screens/states/links.\n   - Finish with: assigned file URL, 03 · Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations. Never claim unfinished work as complete.\n   - FORMATTING (critical): before EVERY tool call, a concise decision summary prefixed exactly 'Reasoning summary:' in the same message; after each tool result, same before next call; final response = 'Reasoning summary: ...' on first line, then 'Final answer:' and the answer.\n   - Unattended session: resolve routine choices from the brief; if blocked, report actual limitation.\n\n   THE 8 FRAMES + REQUIRED LINKS (all now built):\n   - 01_Welcome: FB/Google/mobile/Sign Up buttons, \"Don't have an account?\", headline, 5-portrait collage + heart. Link: Sign Up → 02.\n   - 02_Apple_ID_Sheet: sheet over dimmed 01 clone; close/Logo_Meet/Face ID icon; \"Apple ID\"; body with “sarahp@example.com”; \"Face ID\". Links: Face ID → 03; close → 01.\n   - 03_Explore: header+bell, 9 stories (Your Story+8), 3 post cards (Noemi Slater/Yu Jian/Maddison Burke) with like/comment/more, tab bar Home. Links: Claire story → 05; Dating tab → 04; Profile tab → 07.\n   - 04_Find_Partner: back header, card stack John top + 5 behind, like/pass/super-star buttons, tab bar Dating. Links: back → 03; Home tab → 03; Profile tab → 07.\n   - 05_Friend_Profile: back/Claire Smith/more header, 63K Followers, Follow+Message, Top·Recent·Short tabs, Claire grid 01–09 (01,09 video play). Links: back → 03; Short tab → 06.\n   - 06_Short_Video: full-bleed video, white header back/Short/camera, like 123/comment 89/share/more rail, Yu Jian+Follow, caption, liked-by, music, 4 people, tab bar Home. Link: back → 05.\n   - 07_Profile: menu/Sarah Payne header, 103K Followers, Edit/Share Profile, tabs, Sarah grid 01–09 (01 video), tab bar Profile. Links: menu → 08; Home tab → 03.\n   - 08_Menu: drawer over dimmed 07 clone; close, Logo_Meet, Sarah Payne+Show Profile, 8 menu rows in order. Links: close → 07; Show Profile → 07.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - mcp__figma__use_figma (Plugin API, 50k char limit), get_screenshot (enableBase64Response:true REQUIRED — no shell tool exists in this environment, cannot curl URLs), whoami, get_metadata. get_design_context NOT available.\n   - PROTOTYPE REACTIONS (this runtime's schema — hard-won): `node.reactions = [{trigger:{type:'ON_PRESS'}, actions:[{type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{type:'DISSOLVE', duration:0.25, easing:{type:'EASE_IN_AND_OUT'}}}]}]` — MUST use plural `actions` array (singular `action` errors \"Please update the actions field\"). Trigger must be 'ON_PRESS'|'ON_CLICK'|'ON_HOVER'|'ON_PRESS'|'ON_DRAG'|'ON_MEDIA_END' (NOT 'ON_TAP'). DISSOLVE transition requires easing+duration. `prototypeStartNode` does NOT exist on FrameNode in this runtime — flow start could not be set (limitation).\n   - Icon recoloring: icon components are 24×24 with child VECTORs using STROKES (#1A1A1F); recolor instance children via `inst.findAll(v=>'strokes' in v&&v.strokes.length>0).forEach(v=>{v.strokes=[SOLID(color)]})`. Icon_Facebook 5:14 / Icon_Google 5:10 keep brand colors (never recolor).\n   - whiten() for status bar/home indicator on dark screens: recolor fills+strokes to white by findAll, SKIPPING nodes named containing \"dynamic island\". Status bar 1:33 children: \"9:41\" TEXT (black), \"Dynamic Island\" RECTANGLE (black), \"Signal\" FRAME (fills none), \"Wifi\" ELLIPSE (black), \"Battery\" FRAME (fills none).\n   - Tab bar (component 9:2) active-state overrides per instance: `tbi.findOne(n=>n.name==='i-home')` recolor strokes; labels by name 'l-home','l-dating','l-add','l-chat','l-profile'; Profile avatar ring: `pi2.strokes=[SOLID(P)]; pi2.strokeWeight=2; pi2.strokeAlign='OUTSIDE'`.\n   - Media components have single IMAGE fill scaleMode FILL directly on component — resize instance freely for crop.\n   - Frame cloning for overlay presentations: `bg=f7.clone(); f.appendChild(bg); bg.x=0; bg.y=0; bg.locked=true` then dim rect 0.45.\n   - Fonts: Inter Regular/Medium/Semi Bold/Bold loaded per call via Promise.all; \"Semi Bold\" with space.\n   - Gradients: `{type:'GRADIENT_LINEAR', gradientTransform:[[0,1,0],[-1,0,1]], gradientStops:[{position,color:{r,g,b,a}},...]}` for vertical top→bottom.\n   - Colors: P plum {0.2941,0.0863,0.2980}; OR/acc orchid {0.8667,0.5333,0.8118}; INK {0.102,0.102,0.122}; G gray {0.42,0.42,0.463}; tab-gray {0.557,0.557,0.600}; BG {0.969,0.961,0.973}; W white.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - Figma file vnQfW15mcjOlAJYP4Lrvrx, page 7:2 \"03 · Workspace\" — ALL WORK DELIVERED HERE. Reference pages untouched.\n\n   - CREATED NODE ID MAP (essential):\n     - Tab Bar COMPONENT: 9:2 (placed at 0,-300). Children named: hairline; i-home/i-dating/i-add/i-chat/i-profile (icon instances); c-add (44×44 circle); labels l-home/l-dating/l-add/l-chat/l-profile (10px Medium, w70, y=47). Centers [39.3,117.9,196.5,275.1,353.7]; icons 24 at y=15.\n     - 01_Welcome frame: 9:19. FB button 9:40, Google 9:45, Mobile 9:52, Sign Up 9:55.\n     - 02_Apple_ID_Sheet frame: 9:59; Face ID button 9:88; close icon 9:80.\n     - 03_Explore frame: 9:114; Claire story avatar instance 9:141.\n     - 04_Find_Partner frame: 9:206; back icon 9:218.\n     - 05_Friend_Profile frame: 9:264; back 9:276; Short tab text 9:291.\n     - 06_Short_Video frame: 9:326; back 9:341.\n     - 07_Profile frame: 9:391; menu icon 9:403.\n     - 08_Menu frame: 9:448; drawer 9:478; close 9:481; Show Profile text 9:485.\n     - Hotspot rects (name 'Hotspot', fills []) created inside 03 (2), 04 (2), 05 (1), 07 (1).\n\n   - Frame positions: 01@x0, 02@x450, 03@x900, 04@x1350, 05@x1800, 06@x2250, 07@x2700, 08@x3150, all y=0, 393×852.\n\n   - STANDARD HELPERS used in every build call:\n     ```js\n     const SOLID=(c,o)=>({type:'SOLID',color:c,opacity:o===undefined?1:o});\n     async function ic(id){return await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)}\n     function T(chars,size,style,color,align){const t=figma.createText();t.fontName={family:'Inter',style};t.characters=chars;t.fontSize=size;t.fills=[SOLID(color)];if(align){t.textAlignHorizontal=align}return t}\n     function whiten(n){const skip='dynamic island';n.findAll(c=>{const nm2=c.name.toLowerCase();if(nm2.indexOf(skip)>=0)return false;if('fills' in c&&c.fills&&c.fills.length){c.fills=c.fills.map(x=>x.type==='SOLID'?{type:'SOLID',color:W,opacity:x.opacity===undefined?1:x.opacity}:x)}if('strokes' in c&&c.strokes&&c.strokes.length){c.strokes=c.strokes.map(x=>x.type==='SOLID'?{type:'SOLID',color:W,opacity:x.opacity===undefined?1:x.opacity}:x)}return false})}\n     function wicon(i){i.findAll(v=>'strokes' in v&&v.strokes.length>0).forEach(v=>{v.strokes=[SOLID(W)]})}\n     ```\n\n   - PROTOTYPE WIRING (final working code pattern):\n     ```js\n     const TR={type:'ON_PRESS'};\n     const TRN={type:'DISSOLVE',duration:0.25,easing:{type:'EASE_IN_AND_OUT'}};\n     function nav(dest){return {trigger:TR,actions:[{type:'NODE',destinationId:dest,navigation:'NAVIGATE',transition:TRN}]}}\n     async function link(id,dest){const nd=await ic(id);nd.reactions=[nav(dest)]}\n     function hot(f,x,y,w,h,dest){const r=figma.createRectangle();r.resize(w,h);r.x=x;r.y=y;r.fills=[];r.name='Hotspot';f.appendChild(r);r.reactions=[nav(dest)]}\n     ```\n     Wired: 9:55→9:59; 9:88→9:114; 9:80→9:19; 9:141→9:264; hot(03: 79,770,78,82→9:206; 314,770,79,82→9:391); 9:218→9:114; hot(04: 0,770,79,82→9:114; 314,770,79,82→9:391); 9:276→9:114; hot(05: 290,318,76,36→9:326); 9:341→9:264; 9:403→9:448; hot(07: 0,770,79,82→9:114); 9:481→9:391; 9:485→9:391. All use DISSOLVE 0.25.\n\n   - Key layout data (for fixes): 03 stories x=5.5+i*43 avatar 38 y=102 labels y=146; post cards y=152/352/552, 345×192 r14, photo 345×112 at y+44, actions y+164. 04 card (24,140) 345×516; action buttons ellipses at y=684/688 (56/48px) centers x 112/196.5/281. 05/07 grids cols [24,140,256] rows [366,487,608] tiles 113×118; tabs y=322 underline y=348; buttons y=254. 06 rail x=351 icons 28; info x=16 y 614–735; tab bar (0,770). 08 drawer (83,0) 310×852; rows y=180+i*56.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `node.prototypeStartNode: no such property on FRAME node` when setting flow start on 9:19 → removed the line; flow start not settable in this runtime (report as limitation).\n   - Reactions validation error #1: trigger 'ON_TAP' invalid; action {type:'NODE',destinationId,navigation,transition} rejected with long schema dump listing valid triggers ('ON_CLICK'|'ON_HOVER'|'ON_PRESS'|...) and action literals (CONDITIONAL, BACK/CLOSE, URL, UPDATE_MEDIA_RUNTIME, SET_VARIABLE, SET_VARIABLE_MODE) plus transition needing easing+duration.\n   - Reactions validation error #2: tried {type:'NAVIGATE'...} and fallback shapes — all failed (\"link failed 9:55 -> 9:59\").\n   - FIXED via probe matrix on a scratch rectangle: discovered {type:'NODE', destinationId, navigation:'NAVIGATE', transition:{DISSOLVE,easing,duration}} with trigger ON_PRESS is VALID but must be written as plural `actions` field: \"Please update the `actions` field instead of the `action` field in order to prevent data loss.\" Final wiring with `actions:[...]` succeeded; verified sample reaction JSON returned.\n   - CURRENT UNRESOLVED VISUAL ISSUE: In screenshot of 01_Welcome, the three top buttons (9:40/9:45/9:52) appeared pale/light instead of plum. Diagnostic read returned their fills ARE plum SOLID (r0.294,g0.086,b0.298, opacity 1, visible) with white text fills — data is correct, so appearance may have been a rendering artifact/misread; needs re-screenshot to confirm. Face ID button (fresh instance, same component) rendered plum correctly in 02.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Entire 8-frame design built successfully with all required content, copy verbatim (including curly quotes “sarahp@example.com”), icon recoloring, portrait/media instancing, tab bar component with per-frame active-state overrides, white status-bar glyphs on dark screens (01, 02 bg, 06), video play overlays, card stack with gradient overlay, sheet and drawer presentations via clone+dim.\n   - All 16 required prototype connections wired and confirmed via returned reaction JSON.\n   - Screenshot verification in progress: 01 and 02 reviewed; one issue flagged (button colors) and diagnosed as data-correct.\n   - Remaining verification: 03, 04, 05, 06, 07, 08 screenshots not yet taken.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - “请在以下Figma文件中完成完整设计：Figma 文件：https://www.figma.com/design/vnQfW15mcjOlAJYP4Lrvrx/ 请先阅读「00·Start Here」中的设计任务，参考「01· Foundations」中的视觉规范，复用「02·Components」中的组件，使用「04·Media」中的素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。”\n   (Only user-role message; all other constraints come from the benchmark harness system prompt: use only the assigned file; confirmed account zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai; preserve reference pages; deliver in 03 · Workspace; prefix every tool call with 'Reasoning summary:'; final answer format 'Reasoning summary: ...' + 'Final answer: ...'; unattended session — resolve routine choices from brief, don't wait for human answers; report actual limitations.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   1. Re-screenshot 01_Welcome (9:19) to confirm whether the three top buttons actually render pale or the earlier screenshot was misleading (fills verified plum in data).\n   2. Screenshot and review remaining frames: 03_Explore (9:114), 04_Find_Partner (9:206), 05_Friend_Profile (9:264), 06_Short_Video (9:326), 07_Profile (9:391), 08_Menu (9:448).\n   3. Fix any visible problems found and re-check with screenshots.\n   4. Write final response: 'Reasoning summary:' line, then 'Final answer:' containing assigned file URL (https://www.figma.com/design/vnQfW15mcjOlAJYP4Lrvrx/), 03 · Workspace page ID (7:2), all 8 screen node IDs (9:19, 9:59, 9:114, 9:206, 9:264, 9:326, 9:391, 9:448), prototype work completed (16 connections, list), and remaining limitations (flow start not settable — prototypeStartNode property unsupported in this runtime; any visual caveats).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary: screenshot-verification phase, frame 2 of 8. Screenshots of 9:19 (01_Welcome) and 9:59 (02_Apple_ID_Sheet) were taken inline and reviewed. 02 verified correct (sheet, close, Logo_Meet, Face ID icon, \"Apple ID\", full body copy, plum Face ID button, dimmed 01 background). 01 showed one suspected problem: buttons 9:40/9:45/9:52 appeared pale instead of plum. I then ran a diagnostic use_figma read which returned: component 1:28 fill = plum SOLID; instances 9:40/9:45/9:52 fill = plum SOLID, textFill = white (all